# UI: accessibility & UX (MUST)

- Native/semantic elements first; every control has an accessible name, role and state (`aria-*` / `accessibilityLabel`, `accessibilityRole`, `accessibilityState` / `contentDescription`).
- Colours and spacing only from design tokens (`docs/product/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`); no raw hex values. Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1, UI boundaries ≥ 3:1, in light and dark.
- Targets ≥ 44pt (iOS) / 48dp (Android) / 44px web (never below 24px). Drag actions need a tap alternative.
- Visible focus, logical focus order, focus moves into modals and back to the trigger; focus never hidden behind sticky UI.
- Text scales to 200% / largest Dynamic Type without clipping; never disable font scaling.
- Every screen implements loading, empty, error (with retry, input preserved), offline and success states.
- Forms: visible labels (not placeholders), correct keyboard + autocomplete, inline validation after blur, errors announced.
- Status changes announced via live regions / accessibility announcements. Respect reduced motion.
- One primary action per screen; follow platform navigation (iOS swipe-back, Android back, real URLs on web).

